# Serpentine mixer — the workhorse two-stream diffusive mixer.
#
# Two inlets meet at a junction; the combined stream is folded back and forth
# across the chip six times so the two laminae have time to interdiffuse.
# Length is the only lever a purely diffusive mixer has.

chip "Serpentine mixer"
printer standard-4k
size 40 x 60
base 4
wall 2
edge-spacing 3
split two-piece at 2
channel 0.8 x 0.5 rect

port inletA at 13,54 luer-slip inlet water 10
port inletB at 27,54 luer-slip inlet water 10
port outlet at 20,7  luer-slip outlet

node junction at 20,47
node lead     at 20,43

path inletA -> junction
path inletB -> junction
path junction -> lead

# Six passes at 6 mm row pitch: 5.2 mm of wall between neighbouring runs,
# comfortably above the 2 mm rule.
path lead -> (7,43)
  -> (7,37)  -> (33,37)
  -> (33,31) -> (7,31)
  -> (7,25)  -> (33,25)
  -> (33,19) -> (7,19)
  -> (7,13)  -> (33,13)
  -> (33,7)  -> outlet
